  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Solid fuel used in rocket is a mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math>&nbsp;(in ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>). The heat evolved <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>)</mo></math> per gram of the mixture is _____ (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>840</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AI</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>56</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>27</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Molten iron can be prepared by alumino thermite process as shown below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Al</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Fe</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>The iron oxide and aluminium metal ratio is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;in the above reaction.</p><p>Now, the Enthalpy of the reaction is equal to the difference of enthalpy of formation of products to the&nbsp;enthalpy of formation of reactants.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#916;H</mi><mtext>reaction&#160;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1700</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>840</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>&nbsp;Ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>160</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>54</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>214</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>mixture&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>gm</mi><mtext>&#160;mixture&#160;</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>860</mn></mrow><mn>214</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>gram</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
